% Capability Hardware (CHERI)
% ============================================================
\section{Capability Hardware (CHERI)}\label{sec:cap-cheri}

\subsection{CHERI Architecture}\label{sec:cap-cheri-arch}

The CHERI architecture~\cite{watson2015cheri} extends a conventional RISC
processor (originally MIPS, now also Arm) with hardware capabilities.  Key
design decisions include:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Capability size:} 128 bits (on CHERI-MIPS) or 256 bits (on
      CHERI-Morello/AArch64), including bounds, permissions, address, and tag.
\item \textbf{Tag memory:} A separate tag bit per capability-sized word in
      memory, indicating whether the word contains a valid capability.
\item \textbf{Representable bounds:} The hardware uses a compressed
      representation of bounds to fit within the capability size.  This limits
      the precision of bounds to a set of \emph{representable} values.
\item \textbf{Capability registers:} Some registers are capability registers
      (can hold capabilities with their tags); others are general-purpose
      integer registers.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{CHERI Instruction Extensions}\label{sec:cap-cheri-inst}

CHERI adds new instructions for capability manipulation:

\begin{itemize}
\item \texttt{CLoad}, \texttt{CStore}: Load/store through a capability.
\item \texttt{CSetBounds}, \texttt{CSetBoundsExact}: Narrow the bounds of a
      capability.
\item \texttt{CAndPerm}: Remove permissions from a capability.
\item \texttt{CSeal}, \texttt{CUnseal}: Seal or unseal a capability.
\item \texttt{CGetBase}, \texttt{CGetLen}, \texttt{CGetAddr}: Extract fields
      from a capability.
\item \texttt{CCall}, \texttt{CReturn}: Capability-aware function call and
      return.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{CHERI-Morello}\label{sec:cap-morello}

CHERI-Morello~\cite{watson2020cheri} is a prototype processor implementing CHERI
on the Arm AArch64 architecture.  It demonstrates that capability hardware can
be implemented in a production-quality processor design, with modest area and
power overhead.

